cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this software, please cite it as below."
title: "quant-facts: read-only market analysis with an honest backtest harness"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jafari
    given-names: Sepehr
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aeripsen/quant-facts"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-16"
abstract: >-
  A small toolkit that reports public daily price facts and standard indicators, and replays a
  simple rule with next-bar execution, a chronological train/test split, costs, and a printed
  account of what the parameter search cost (multiple-testing haircut, deflated Sharpe,
  probability of backtest overfitting, walk-forward with a frozen control). A boundary in code
  stops the tool from producing advice; the run fails rather than print it.
keywords:
  - backtesting
  - overfitting
  - multiple testing
  - deflated sharpe ratio
  - walk-forward
